It's a cute idea, but I think that hacking off body parts goes against
the spirit of both AD&D and Nethack. Hit points do not necessarily
represent physical damage (although they might!). The represent how
long you can keep fighting, against injury, exaustion, mental fatigue,
etc. If you have 50 HP, and a monster brings you down to 3, it might
have done so without giving you a scratch. Then, you are too tired
to block a stroke, or your body is too tired to endure a shock,
and you die. Losing a limb would effectively mean dying anyway, since
the monster would be able to finish you off pretty effectively.

